\paragraph{Sensitivity to $\rho$.}
The inter-pair SCS correlation $\rho = 0.35$ is estimated from pairs sharing a common type. At $\rho = 0.20$ (halved correlation), a parallel simulation yields batch $R^2 \approx 0.22$, still matching the observed value; at $\rho = 0.50$, the correlation structure approaches the positive-definiteness boundary, suggesting $\rho = 0.35$ sits in a stable regime. The simulation is illustrative; the observed batch $R^2 = 0.218$ is the primary evidence.

